<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="Client" id="grpc-client">

    <p>
        <code>GrpcClient</code> connects to a gRPC server and provides service stubs via <code>withService</code>.
    </p>
    <code-block lang="Kotlin">
        import kotlinx.io.bytestring.ByteString
        import kotlinx.rpc.grpc.client.GrpcClient
        import kotlinx.rpc.withService
        import ImageRecognizer
        import invoke

        val client = GrpcClient("localhost", 8080) {
            credentials = plaintext()
        }

        val recognizer = client.withService&lt;ImageRecognizer&gt;()

        val image = Image {
            data = ByteString(0, 1, 2, 3)
        }
        val result = recognizer.recognize(image)
    </code-block>

    <chapter title="Configuration" id="grpc-client-configuration">
        <deflist>
            <def title="credentials">
                Sets client credentials. Use <code>plaintext()</code> for insecure connections (testing only)
                or <code>tls { ... }</code> for secure communication.
                Default TLS credentials are used when not specified.
            </def>
            <def title="messageMarshallerResolver">
                A <code>GrpcMarshallerResolver</code> for custom serialization.
                Not needed when using generated Protobuf types.
                See <a href="grpc-services.topic" anchor="no-proto"/>.
            </def>
            <def title="overrideAuthority">
                Overrides the authority used with TLS and HTTP virtual hosting.
                Does not change the actual host the client connects to.
            </def>
            <def title="intercept(...)">
                Adds client-side interceptors.
                Interceptors are executed in the order they are added.
            </def>
            <def title="keepAlive { ... }">
                Configures keep-alive pings to detect broken connections.
                Pings are disabled by default (<code>time = Duration.INFINITE</code>),
                with a 20-second response timeout and <code>withoutCalls = false</code>.
            </def>
            <def title="userAgent">
                An application User-Agent prefix, followed by the gRPC runtime's own token.
                Defaults to <code>null</code>, which sends only the runtime token.
            </def>
            <def title="maxInboundMessageSize">
                The maximum size, in bytes, of an inbound message.
                Larger messages are rejected with <code>RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED</code>.
                Defaults to 4 MiB (4,194,304 bytes).
            </def>
            <def title="maxInboundMetadataSize">
                The maximum size, in bytes, of inbound metadata.
                Defaults to 8 KiB (8,192 bytes).
            </def>
            <def title="idleTimeout">
                The duration without ongoing RPCs before the client enters idle mode and closes its
                connections. A new RPC takes the client out of idle mode.
                <code>Duration.INFINITE</code> disables automatic idle mode.
                Defaults to 30 minutes.
            </def>
        </deflist>
        <note>
            Duration options (<code>idleTimeout</code> and <code>keepAlive</code>) accept
            <code>Duration.INFINITE</code> to disable the behavior. Finite values must be under
            <code>Int.MAX_VALUE</code> milliseconds (about 24.8 days).
            On Kotlin/Native these become gRPC channel arguments, whose values are a C
            <code>int</code>. <code>Duration.INFINITE</code> is passed as
            <code>Int.MAX_VALUE</code>, the largest value such an argument can hold and the one
            gRPC treats as effectively unbounded, so a finite value must stay below it to remain
            distinguishable. The bound is enforced on every platform so that the same
            configuration behaves identically everywhere; out-of-range values throw
            <code>IllegalArgumentException</code>.
        </note>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Call options" id="grpc-client-call-options">
        <p>
            The per-call <code>GrpcCallOptions.waitForReady</code> option defaults to <code>null</code>.
            This uses the channel's default behavior: calls fail when the channel
            is in transient failure, unless a service configuration delivered by the name resolver
            enables waiting for that method. Set <code>true</code> to wait for a connection, or
            <code>false</code> to override a service configuration that enables waiting.
        </p>
        <p>
            <code>GrpcCallOptions.timeout</code> defaults to <code>null</code> (no deadline).
            Set a timeout when enabling wait-for-ready to bound how long the call may wait.
        </p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Lifecycle" id="grpc-client-lifecycle">
        <p>
            Call <code>shutdown()</code> to stop accepting new calls and <code>awaitTermination()</code>
            to wait for in-flight calls to complete.
            Use <code>shutdownNow()</code> to cancel all calls immediately.
        </p>
    </chapter>
</topic>
